But a leg?

1407
00:48:20,840 --> 00:48:21,760
No, I mean...

1408
00:48:21,760 --> 00:48:24,720
Maybe his animal form drops a tail.

1409
00:48:24,720 --> 00:48:26,160
So as a human,

1410
00:48:26,160 --> 00:48:28,040
maybe he drops a leg?

1411
00:48:28,100 --> 00:48:31,420
(So what's the password?)

1412
00:48:33,900 --> 00:48:36,740
(Picks up the box again)

1413
00:48:37,600 --> 00:48:39,040
The saw.

1414
00:48:39,400 --> 00:48:40,800
So even missing a leg,

1415
00:48:40,800 --> 00:48:42,800
he still pulled the breaker.

1416
00:48:42,800 --> 00:48:43,600
His animal trait.

1417
00:48:43,600 --> 00:48:45,400
He can drop a limb.
What animal does that?

1418
00:48:45,680 --> 00:48:46,600
Lizard.

1419
00:48:46,600 --> 00:48:48,200
Gecko.

1420
00:48:48,220 --> 00:48:49,940
(Animal trait)

1421
00:48:49,940 --> 00:48:52,980
(Tui Haowan only, Trait)

1422
00:48:54,340 --> 00:48:55,660
(Unlocked)

1423
00:48:56,240 --> 00:48:57,080
It opened!

1424
00:48:57,080 --> 00:48:58,680
Gecko?

1425
00:48:59,520 --> 00:49:00,520
Regeneration.

1426
00:49:00,960 --> 00:49:01,720
Regeneration?

1427
00:49:01,920 --> 00:49:02,480
Seriously?

1428
00:49:02,480 --> 00:49:04,400
How'd you get "regeneration"?

1429
00:49:04,400 --> 00:49:05,320
Gecko. Regeneration.

1430
00:49:07,080 --> 00:49:07,800
That's smart!

1431
00:49:07,820 --> 00:49:09,000
(First to crack it)

1432
00:49:09,000 --> 00:49:09,680
Am I the killer?

1433
00:49:10,400 --> 00:49:11,680
No.

1434
00:49:12,400 --> 00:49:14,160
So he dropped his own arm

1435
00:49:14,160 --> 00:49:16,200
for the scare.

1436
00:49:16,200 --> 00:49:16,600
Right.

1437
00:49:19,720 --> 00:49:21,080
This is the vitals monitor, right?

1438
00:49:22,200 --> 00:49:23,560
(Alert: Heartbeat stopped)
It stopped at 3PM.

1439
00:49:24,080 --> 00:49:27,920
At 3PM, I'll pull the main breaker.

1440
00:49:28,080 --> 00:49:30,280
So, he died at 3PM.

1441
00:49:30,280 --> 00:49:31,060
(Case summary, Victim: Tui Haowan)

1442
00:49:31,060 --> 00:49:31,820
(Location: Courtyard,
Death: 22 June, 3PM)

1443
00:49:31,820 --> 00:49:32,540
(Cause: Unknown)

1444
00:49:33,160 --> 00:49:33,800
What's this?

1445
00:49:34,600 --> 00:49:35,520
Buy one, get one free.

1446
00:49:35,520 --> 00:49:37,720
Special-spectrum light.

1447
00:49:38,160 --> 00:49:40,680
I'm shining this everywhere.

1448
00:49:40,680 --> 00:49:41,880
Maybe it reveals something.

1449
00:49:42,460 --> 00:49:43,480
(Nothing)

1450
00:49:43,480 --> 00:49:44,680
Let me read this.

1451
00:49:45,480 --> 00:49:46,560
Top graduate file.

1452
00:49:47,080 --> 00:49:49,400
(Top Graduate File)
Tui Haowan's real name is Huo Xiyi.

1453
00:49:49,720 --> 00:49:52,040
His trait is severed limbs regenerate.

1454
00:49:52,040 --> 00:49:54,080
Good for high-risk jobs.

1455
00:49:56,560 --> 00:49:57,640
He can see UV light

1456
00:49:57,640 --> 00:50:01,000
others can't.

1457
00:50:01,280 --> 00:50:03,480
(Tui Haowan can see UV light)
He sees UV light?

1458
00:50:05,880 --> 00:50:07,800
Here's the breaker diagram.

1459
00:50:08,480 --> 00:50:12,040
The left breaker leaks current.

1460
00:50:12,040 --> 00:50:13,320
Touch the wrong one, you die.

1461
00:50:13,320 --> 00:50:15,760
I had Bu Kakao leave

1462
00:50:15,760 --> 00:50:18,120
a mark only I can see.

1463
00:50:18,120 --> 00:50:19,360
So I won't pull the wrong one.

1464
00:50:19,920 --> 00:50:21,840
If you pull the faulty one,

1465
00:50:21,840 --> 00:50:22,960
it shorts out

1466
00:50:22,960 --> 00:50:24,880
and trips the main breaker.

1467
00:50:24,880 --> 00:50:25,880
So he was electrocuted.

1468
00:50:25,880 --> 00:50:26,240
Right.

1469
00:50:26,240 --> 00:50:27,260
(Cause of death: Electrocution)

1470
00:50:27,560 --> 00:50:29,400
Wasn't one breaker burned out?

1471
00:50:31,120 --> 00:50:32,720
Did someone swap them?

1472
00:50:33,920 --> 00:50:35,600
Maybe they swapped them.

1473
00:50:35,600 --> 00:50:36,800
They moved the left one

1474
00:50:36,800 --> 00:50:37,760
to the middle,

1475
00:50:37,760 --> 00:50:39,120
where Tui Haowan would pull.

1476
00:50:39,140 --> 00:50:41,020
(Jin Goffy: The killer swapped
the breakers)

1477
00:50:41,020 --> 00:50:42,860
(Tui Haowan pulled
the live one and died)

1478
00:50:44,720 --> 00:50:45,960
Can we check that file?

1479
00:50:46,720 --> 00:50:47,760
Yeah.

1480
00:50:48,020 --> 00:50:48,800
(Say a keyword)

1481
00:50:48,800 --> 00:50:49,880
(Records found)
Huo Xiyi.

1482
00:50:51,080 --> 00:50:52,480
Physical Marvels.

1483
00:50:52,720 --> 00:50:54,720
In the world of Animal Planet,

1484
00:50:54,720 --> 00:50:56,520
many species have

1485
00:50:56,520 --> 00:50:59,760
physical traits even
advanced humans envy.

1486
00:51:00,120 --> 00:51:01,240
Got it. This is important.

1487
00:51:01,240 --> 00:51:02,160
Here are the categories.

1488
00:51:02,480 --> 00:51:05,560
Category A: Soft-body mimicry.

1489
00:51:05,560 --> 00:51:06,280
Examples:

1490
00:51:06,280 --> 00:51:08,280
mimic octopuses and black sea cucumbers.

1491
00:51:08,760 --> 00:51:10,120
For extreme regeneration, we've got

1492
00:51:10,120 --> 00:51:12,160
geckos and salamanders.

1493
00:51:12,360 --> 00:51:14,400
Then there's visual range.

1494
00:51:14,400 --> 00:51:15,440
This one's important, guys.

1495
00:51:15,440 --> 00:51:18,680
Beyond the visible spectrum:
canines and reindeer.

1496
00:51:18,680 --> 00:51:19,680
Their retinas can detect

1497
00:51:19,680 --> 00:51:21,280
what humans can't see.

1498
00:51:21,720 --> 00:51:23,920
Short-wave ultraviolet light.

1499
00:51:23,920 --> 00:51:25,280
Their world is full of

1500
00:51:25,280 --> 00:51:27,200
invisible road maps

1501
00:51:27,200 --> 00:51:28,480
formed by fluorescent

1502
00:51:28,480 --> 00:51:30,200
urine trails.

1503
00:51:31,640 --> 00:51:33,080
Canines have

1504
00:51:33,080 --> 00:51:35,800
strong low-light vision.

1505
00:51:36,240 --> 00:51:38,280
But with no light at all,

1506
00:51:38,280 --> 00:51:39,920
canines can't see either.

1507
00:51:40,240 --> 00:51:42,760
(Ke: Low-light vision)
Next category: night vision.

1508
00:51:42,760 --> 00:51:44,680
For example, rabbits and cats.

1509
00:51:44,680 --> 00:51:45,360
Rabbits.

1510
00:51:45,360 --> 00:51:46,480
Their eyes contain

1511
00:51:46,480 --> 00:51:48,920
large numbers of rod cells.

1512
00:51:48,920 --> 00:51:50,240
In dim environments,

1513
00:51:50,240 --> 00:51:52,040
they have excellent night vision,

1514
00:51:52,040 --> 00:51:54,440
so they can roam at night or dusk.

1515
00:51:54,540 --> 00:51:56,280
(Ke: Low-light vision.
Nan: Excellent night vision)

1516
00:51:56,280 --> 00:51:57,320
(Canine)
He's a canine.

1517
00:51:57,320 --> 00:51:58,160
(Rabbit)
This one's a rabbit.

1518
00:51:58,880 --> 00:52:01,240
(Has night vision)
They can walk in the dark.

1519
00:52:03,000 --> 00:52:05,320
That 15-minute blackout.

1520
00:52:05,320 --> 00:52:06,560
So you were the one who disappeared.

1521
00:52:06,580 --> 00:52:09,540
(The suspects start tearing
into each other)

1522
00:52:09,560 --> 00:52:10,760
Some creatures on Animal Planet

1523
00:52:10,760 --> 00:52:11,760
are incredible mimics.

1524
00:52:11,760 --> 00:52:14,000
They copy sounds
and emotions to seem human.

1525
00:52:14,000 --> 00:52:15,480
Sound mimicry: mynas and lyrebirds.

1526
00:52:15,480 --> 00:52:17,040
Then there's lure camouflage.

1527
00:52:17,040 --> 00:52:18,600
Anglerfish and orchid mantises.

1528
00:52:18,600 --> 00:52:20,160
That probably doesn't apply to us.

1529
00:52:20,260 --> 00:52:21,040
(Ke: Low-light vision)

1530
00:52:21,040 --> 00:52:21,840
(Nan: Excellent night vision)
I'm ruled out again.

1531
00:52:21,840 --> 00:52:22,720
(Jin: No night vision)

1532
00:52:22,720 --> 00:52:23,680
(He: Unknown)
I'm ruled out.

1533
00:52:23,680 --> 00:52:25,160
You're a canine, Ke.

1534
00:52:25,160 --> 00:52:26,120
Right, I'm ruled out.

1535
00:52:26,120 --> 00:52:27,080
You're nocturnal.

1536
00:52:27,080 --> 00:52:28,240
I can't see at night.

1537
00:52:28,240 --> 00:52:29,320
No, look.

1538
00:52:29,320 --> 00:52:32,000
They can form an invisible road map.

1539
00:52:32,000 --> 00:52:33,000
That makes you a prime suspect.

1540
00:52:33,200 --> 00:52:34,400
Wait, what?

1541
00:52:34,400 --> 00:52:35,560
(Ke: Low-light. Nan: Night vision)
You two, then.

1542
00:52:35,560 --> 00:52:36,200
(Jin: No night vision. He: Unknown)
You two.

1543
00:52:37,280 --> 00:52:38,400
Tell us the truth.

1544
00:52:38,460 --> 00:52:39,280
(Prime suspect)

1545
00:52:39,280 --> 00:52:41,360
Do you have night vision?

1546
00:52:41,600 --> 00:52:42,400
Don't laugh.

1547
00:52:42,880 --> 00:52:44,400
You can't even hide that grin.

1548
00:52:44,400 --> 00:52:45,960
(Naturally upturned lips, okay?)
I just smile a lot.

1549
00:52:45,960 --> 00:52:47,920
She's pretty convincing too.

1550
00:52:48,200 --> 00:52:48,760
Me?

1551
00:52:48,760 --> 00:52:49,320
(Four-way bickering)

1552
00:52:49,320 --> 00:52:49,800
Yeah.

1553
00:52:50,720 --> 00:52:52,480
This time, let's vote for...

1554
00:52:53,320 --> 00:52:54,640
I don't know anything.

1555
00:52:54,960 --> 00:52:56,160
I'd be no human if I lied.

1556
00:52:57,800 --> 00:52:59,840
That oath is technically true today.

1557
00:52:59,840 --> 00:53:00,360
That doesn't count.

1558
00:53:00,360 --> 00:53:01,520
We've all sworn worse.

1559
00:53:01,760 --> 00:53:03,200
(Sincerely)
I really want to be the killer.

1560
00:53:04,200 --> 00:53:05,400
We've all used that one.

1561
00:53:08,680 --> 00:53:10,120
We all make deadly oaths. Seriously.

1562
00:53:10,480 --> 00:53:11,320
Jin Goofy,

1563
00:53:11,320 --> 00:53:12,320
you don't believe me?

1564
00:53:12,320 --> 00:53:14,040
Don't play the sympathy card. Not here.

1565
00:53:14,500 --> 00:53:17,180
(Jin, don't you miss me?)

1566
00:53:17,200 --> 00:53:18,440
You're not off the hook either.

1567
00:53:19,240 --> 00:53:21,080
What family are capybaras in?

1568
00:53:21,080 --> 00:53:22,000
I honestly don't know.

1569
00:53:22,680 --> 00:53:24,280
What family are capybaras in?

1570
00:53:24,300 --> 00:53:25,820
(Capybaras belong to...?)

1571
00:53:27,920 --> 00:53:29,200
Keep framing people.

1572
00:53:29,200 --> 00:53:30,160
Who, me?

1573
00:53:30,560 --> 00:53:31,240
Me?

1574
00:53:31,240 --> 00:53:32,080
I'm a capybara.

1575
00:53:32,080 --> 00:53:33,360
How could I move around at night?

1576
00:53:34,800 --> 00:53:35,440
What family?

1577
00:53:35,760 --> 00:53:37,880
We probably only know canines, felines,

1578
00:53:37,880 --> 00:53:38,560
and a few others.

1579
00:53:38,560 --> 00:53:39,480
He and you

1580
00:53:39,480 --> 00:53:41,000
aren't listed here yet,

1581
00:53:41,000 --> 00:53:42,320
so you're not ruled out.

1582
00:53:42,320 --> 00:53:43,800
We can't use this to clear anyone.

1583
00:53:43,800 --> 00:53:44,760
It doesn't rule people out.

1584
00:53:44,760 --> 00:53:45,720
But it can...

1585
00:53:45,720 --> 00:53:46,440
Narrow down the killer.

1586
00:53:46,460 --> 00:53:48,500
(Night-vision user,
low-light vision user)

1587
00:53:49,280 --> 00:53:50,080
That's what I mean.

1588
00:53:50,080 --> 00:53:51,400
Can you stop accusing everyone?

1589
00:53:51,400 --> 00:53:51,920
Exactly.

1590
00:53:51,920 --> 00:53:52,880
You two.

1591
00:53:53,560 --> 00:53:55,280
You two are working together.

1592
00:53:55,280 --> 00:53:56,560
One played with my feelings.

1593
00:53:56,560 --> 00:53:57,600
The other played with hers.

1594
00:53:57,780 --> 00:53:59,000
(Four-way fight)

1595
00:53:59,000 --> 00:54:00,640
Nice job turning it back on us.

1596
00:54:00,920 --> 00:54:02,240
I trust my brother.

1597
00:54:02,240 --> 00:54:03,800
I bet one clue is

1598
00:54:03,800 --> 00:54:04,960
(Investigation zone, accusation zone)
what this light can reveal.

1599
00:54:04,960 --> 00:54:05,400
Reveal...

1600
00:54:05,460 --> 00:54:07,260
(What's the spectral light for?)

1601
00:54:11,860 --> 00:54:12,900
(The breaker left
of the main switch is live)

1602
00:54:12,900 --> 00:54:13,980
(Touch it and you die)

1603
00:54:13,980 --> 00:54:15,020
(I had Bu Kakao mark it
with a sign only I'd know)

1604
00:54:15,020 --> 00:54:16,060
(It reveals UV light
other creatures can't see)

1605
00:54:16,480 --> 00:54:17,960
Let's check the breaker box.

1606
00:54:17,960 --> 00:54:19,280
Let's see if they were switched.

1607
00:54:20,000 --> 00:54:20,360
Let's go.

1608
00:54:21,680 --> 00:54:22,120
Shine it here.

1609
00:54:26,080 --> 00:54:27,360
Here. Down here. Look.

1610
00:54:28,320 --> 00:54:29,640
Do not touch. Electric shock hazard.

1611
00:54:31,360 --> 00:54:31,960
So that's it.

1612
00:54:31,960 --> 00:54:32,560
He said

1613
00:54:32,560 --> 00:54:35,600
the breaker left
of the main switch was live.

1614
00:54:35,600 --> 00:54:36,240
Touch it and you die.

1615
00:54:36,240 --> 00:54:37,800
So this is the live one.

1616
00:54:37,800 --> 00:54:39,000
(Do not touch. Electric shock hazard)
He meant to pull this one,

1617
00:54:39,000 --> 00:54:40,400
(Fictional scene. Do not imitate)
but pulled the live one instead.

1618
00:54:40,400 --> 00:54:41,720
(Live breaker, main switch)
That's because the warning label

1619
00:54:41,720 --> 00:54:43,560
was originally under the live breaker.

1620
00:54:43,560 --> 00:54:45,920
The killer moved it
one space to the left,

1621
00:54:45,920 --> 00:54:47,720
making Tui Haowan
mistake the live breaker

1622
00:54:47,720 --> 00:54:48,640
for the main switch.

1623
00:54:51,280 --> 00:54:52,520
(Fictional scene. Do not imitate)
Pulling the live breaker

1624
00:54:52,520 --> 00:54:53,240
(Live breaker, main switch)
causes a short circuit,

1625
00:54:53,240 --> 00:54:54,400
which trips the main switch.

1626
00:54:54,400 --> 00:54:55,840
(Main switch shuts off automatically)
That's why this flipped down.

1627
00:54:55,840 --> 00:54:56,160
Right.

1628
00:54:56,160 --> 00:54:57,440
He was electrocuted
the moment he pulled it.

1629
00:54:57,440 --> 00:54:58,200
Then his body was here.

1630
00:54:58,200 --> 00:54:59,560
During those 15 minutes,
the killer came over

1631
00:54:59,560 --> 00:55:01,560
(Body disposed)
and threw the whole body inside.

1632
00:55:03,800 --> 00:55:04,640
That solves it.

1633
00:55:04,640 --> 00:55:06,320
We've figured out
how the murder happened.

1634
00:55:06,320 --> 00:55:07,680
So now we can...

1635
00:55:08,000 --> 00:55:08,640
What?

1636
00:55:08,640 --> 00:55:10,520
Nail the killer.

1637
00:55:10,520 --> 00:55:12,080
Who?

1638
00:55:12,080 --> 00:55:12,960
No, I was kidding.

1639
00:55:12,960 --> 00:55:14,880
We still need to work out the timeline.

1640
00:55:14,880 --> 00:55:15,680
What's this?

1641
00:55:18,040 --> 00:55:18,880
It's fur.

1642
00:55:18,880 --> 00:55:19,440
Fur?

1643
00:55:19,680 --> 00:55:21,280
Is it capybara fur?

1644
00:55:21,300 --> 00:55:23,180
(Another fight is about to begin)

1645
00:55:25,920 --> 00:55:28,320
You just blew away the key evidence!

1646
00:55:28,320 --> 00:55:29,040
Shedding fur?

1647
00:55:29,040 --> 00:55:31,320
We found key evidence against you.

1648
00:55:36,080 --> 00:55:37,440
Remember what you just said.

1649
00:55:37,440 --> 00:55:38,400
Record it. Say it again.

1650
00:55:38,400 --> 00:55:39,440
Come on. What did you say?

1651
00:55:39,440 --> 00:55:41,080
I said we found

1652
00:55:41,080 --> 00:55:42,880
key evidence against He Struggle.

1653
00:55:42,880 --> 00:55:44,040
And who found it?

1654
00:55:44,880 --> 00:55:46,240
No, let's think this through.

1655
00:55:46,240 --> 00:55:46,600
Let's look again.

1656
00:55:46,600 --> 00:55:47,120
(Reason returns)
Look again.

1657
00:55:47,120 --> 00:55:47,640
Is this even fur?

1658
00:55:48,680 --> 00:55:49,400
See it?

1659
00:55:49,400 --> 00:55:50,400
This fur definitely isn't...

1660
00:55:50,400 --> 00:55:51,200
It's definitely not.

1661
00:55:52,600 --> 00:55:53,640
His fur is brown.

1662
00:55:53,920 --> 00:55:54,320
Look.

1663
00:55:55,120 --> 00:55:56,880
See who still trusts me?

1664
00:55:57,240 --> 00:55:58,440
(Fictional scene. Do not imitate)
Wait, let me check the capybara.

1665
00:56:00,600 --> 00:56:01,760
Its fur is brown.

1666
00:56:01,760 --> 00:56:03,400
There was fur in her diary.

1667
00:56:03,400 --> 00:56:05,200
(Reddish brown with a brown belly)
It was that long brown kind.

1668
00:56:05,200 --> 00:56:05,880
Long fur.

1669
00:56:07,000 --> 00:56:07,600
Keep looking.

1670
00:56:08,200 --> 00:56:08,880
Search!

1671
00:56:08,880 --> 00:56:10,040
Find it for me!

1672
00:56:10,440 --> 00:56:11,680
I'll remember the three of you

1673
00:56:11,680 --> 00:56:13,120
and the faces you made just now.

1674
00:56:13,520 --> 00:56:13,920
Okay.

1675
00:56:14,020 --> 00:56:17,840
(Honk, honk, honk)

1676
00:56:17,840 --> 00:56:18,920
Okay.

1677
00:56:19,120 --> 00:56:19,760
Could there be

1678
00:56:19,760 --> 00:56:21,080
another key clue here?

1679
00:56:21,140 --> 00:56:23,860
(Only thinking about key clues)

1680
00:56:28,280 --> 00:56:29,040
What's this?

1681
00:56:29,040 --> 00:56:29,760
It's fur.

1682
00:56:30,560 --> 00:56:31,320
It really is fur.

1683
00:56:32,030 --> 00:56:33,720
♪There's fur by the door♪

1684
00:56:34,060 --> 00:56:35,480
♪The water's full of fur♪

1685
00:56:35,480 --> 00:56:36,040
No, wait.

1686
00:56:36,040 --> 00:56:37,560
We're obsessed with this fur now.

1687
00:56:37,560 --> 00:56:38,480
Everything looks like fur.

1688
00:56:38,480 --> 00:56:40,360
No, it really is fur, Ding.

1689
00:56:40,360 --> 00:56:41,400
This is definitely fur.

1690
00:56:41,400 --> 00:56:42,320
Is it mine?

1691
00:56:43,560 --> 00:56:44,480
I don't shed.

1692
00:56:46,280 --> 00:56:47,200
It really is fur.

1693
00:56:47,680 --> 00:56:49,040
Wait. Feel around.

1694
00:56:49,040 --> 00:56:49,720
Is there something underneath?

1695
00:56:50,480 --> 00:56:51,000
The two of us...

1696
00:56:51,000 --> 00:56:51,600
Wait. What's this?

1697
00:56:54,080 --> 00:56:54,960
A leaf.

1698
00:56:54,960 --> 00:56:55,960
A leaf. That makes sense.

1699
00:56:57,360 --> 00:56:59,320
We scared ourselves.

1700
00:56:59,520 --> 00:57:01,720
We've lost it, searching
for crucial evidence.

1701
00:57:18,720 --> 00:57:19,200
What's this?

1702
00:57:21,000 --> 00:57:21,680
Glasses.

1703
00:57:22,120 --> 00:57:23,040
They're broken.

1704
00:57:30,680 --> 00:57:32,560
(Press the matching number)
To open the matching locker.

1705
00:57:33,960 --> 00:57:35,680
The doors behind us can open.

1706
00:57:36,200 --> 00:57:37,080
It's locked.

1707
00:57:37,640 --> 00:57:38,990
Oh my God.

1708
00:57:39,880 --> 00:57:41,560
We can't get out! The door's locked!

1709
00:57:41,880 --> 00:57:42,960
So one of the six of us

1710
00:57:42,960 --> 00:57:44,400
opened their own door.

1711
00:57:44,920 --> 00:57:45,920
Then they came out.

1712
00:57:46,320 --> 00:57:48,040
They used those 15 minutes to do this.

1713
00:57:48,580 --> 00:57:49,640
(Night vision goggles)

1714
00:57:49,640 --> 00:57:51,040
Night vision goggles.

1715
00:57:51,360 --> 00:57:53,520
Could this rule someone out?

1716
00:57:53,520 --> 00:57:55,160
It rules out anyone with night vision.

1717
00:57:55,160 --> 00:57:56,840
They can already see in the dark.

1718
00:57:56,840 --> 00:57:57,200
Right.

1719
00:57:57,200 --> 00:57:57,800
They wouldn't use these.

1720
00:57:57,800 --> 00:57:58,440
They wouldn't need them.

1721
00:57:58,440 --> 00:57:59,840
Then you're definitely cleared.

1722
00:58:00,080 --> 00:58:00,960
(Ke: Low-light vision)
Because I can see.

1723
00:58:00,960 --> 00:58:01,600
(Nan: Excellent night vision)
We don't need them.

1724
00:58:01,600 --> 00:58:02,320
(Jin: No night vision)
Right.

1725
00:58:02,400 --> 00:58:03,920
(He: Unknown)
Then I'm locked in.

1726
00:58:03,980 --> 00:58:05,180
(Suspicion rising)

1727
00:58:05,800 --> 00:58:07,840
I just remembered. I'm a canine too.

1728
00:58:08,400 --> 00:58:10,160
Now you're a canine?

1729
00:58:11,080 --> 00:58:13,200
What kind of canine are you?

1730
00:58:13,200 --> 00:58:14,600
It's definitely him!

1731
00:58:14,600 --> 00:58:15,280
(Maximum suspicion toward her boyfriend)

1732
00:58:15,280 --> 00:58:16,880
Because they never introduced him.

1733
00:58:17,120 --> 00:58:19,040
They mentioned the fish, pipa, and dog.

1734
00:58:19,040 --> 00:58:20,360
They mentioned the rabbit too.

1735
00:58:20,960 --> 00:58:22,760
Only the capybara wasn't mentioned.

1736
00:58:22,760 --> 00:58:23,440
Nan,

1737
00:58:24,080 --> 00:58:25,080
don't trust

1738
00:58:25,080 --> 00:58:26,440
Jin right now.

1739
00:58:26,680 --> 00:58:28,280
Of course I trust her.

1740
00:58:28,280 --> 00:58:28,960
Wait, guys.

1741
00:58:28,960 --> 00:58:29,560
There's a trash can.

1742
00:58:29,560 --> 00:58:30,360
Let's see what's inside.

1743
00:58:31,500 --> 00:58:33,100
(Push)

1744
00:58:37,400 --> 00:58:38,320
There's a phone.

1745
00:58:39,440 --> 00:58:41,080
Tui Haowan's phone.

1746
00:58:41,080 --> 00:58:42,620
(Tui Haowan)

1747
00:58:42,880 --> 00:58:44,400
There's a contact named Bu Kakao.

1748
00:58:44,400 --> 00:58:45,640
They sent him a message.

1749
00:58:45,640 --> 00:58:47,200
(Bu Kakao, June 21, 2026, 3PM)
It's from June 21,

1750
00:58:47,200 --> 00:58:47,680
3PM

1751
00:58:47,840 --> 00:58:48,760
Bu,

1752
00:58:48,760 --> 00:58:50,000
later, do exactly as I say.

1753
00:58:50,000 --> 00:58:52,280
Mark the courtyard's breaker box.

1754
00:58:52,280 --> 00:58:53,360
Make sure you use

1755
00:58:53,360 --> 00:58:55,560
a UV mark no one else can see.

1756
00:58:55,560 --> 00:58:57,040
A UV mark no one else can see.

1757
00:58:57,040 --> 00:58:58,800
Those were the words
from earlier, right?

1758
00:58:58,800 --> 00:58:59,360
Yes.

1759
00:58:59,360 --> 00:59:00,720
(Do not touch. Electric shock hazard.)
Don't worry, boss.

1760
00:59:00,720 --> 00:59:02,640
I never get stuck on a job.

1761
00:59:03,600 --> 00:59:05,000
Not everyone can see

1762
00:59:05,000 --> 00:59:06,720
UV markings like I can.

1763
00:59:06,720 --> 00:59:08,280
If you can't see the mark,

1764
00:59:08,280 --> 00:59:09,680
come to my office first.

1765
00:59:09,680 --> 00:59:10,760
In the second drawer,

1766
00:59:10,760 --> 00:59:13,480
get the spectral lamp and breaker key.

1767
00:59:14,320 --> 00:59:15,760
There's a key and a lamp.

1768
00:59:15,760 --> 00:59:17,000
I don't need those.

1769
00:59:17,400 --> 00:59:18,640
I can place it properly.

1770
00:59:18,640 --> 00:59:19,800
I promise I won't get stuck.

1771
00:59:20,280 --> 00:59:21,520
I know who this is.

1772
00:59:21,520 --> 00:59:23,000
The guy who led us earlier.

1773
00:59:23,000 --> 00:59:23,880
He's from Tianjin.

1774
00:59:24,320 --> 00:59:25,840
Things are about to get dangerous.

1775
00:59:25,840 --> 00:59:27,040
Just run with me.

1776
00:59:28,360 --> 00:59:29,800
Why are you talking to me?

1777
00:59:32,360 --> 00:59:35,160
Good. Everything's going
according to plan.

1778
00:59:35,760 --> 00:59:37,640
At tomorrow's crazy animal theme party,

1779
00:59:37,640 --> 00:59:39,600
I'm gonna show them a real thrill!

1780
00:59:39,880 --> 00:59:40,920
Boss,

1781
00:59:40,920 --> 00:59:41,840
remember,

1782
00:59:41,840 --> 00:59:43,280
to the right of the label

1783
00:59:43,280 --> 00:59:44,800
is the main breaker.

1784
00:59:45,440 --> 00:59:47,400
Pull it to turn the lights on or off.

1785
00:59:47,400 --> 00:59:49,080
Don't pull the wrong one.

1786
00:59:49,080 --> 00:59:50,120
It's dangerous!

1787
00:59:50,120 --> 00:59:51,960
The far-right one was burned earlier.

1788
00:59:51,960 --> 00:59:54,680
I know. Get back to work.

1789
00:59:55,120 --> 00:59:57,600
Also, stay away from that stinky bear,

1790
00:59:57,600 --> 00:59:58,280
Tai Kule.

1791
00:59:58,760 --> 01:00:00,120
Something's off about him.

1792
01:00:00,680 --> 01:00:01,440
That boss from today.

1793
01:00:01,440 --> 01:00:02,560
The client, right?

1794
01:00:02,560 --> 01:00:03,440
Yeah, a major client.

1795
01:00:03,440 --> 01:00:04,280
Tai Kule.

1796
01:00:06,200 --> 01:00:07,480
Is there a photo album?

1797
01:00:07,540 --> 01:00:08,360
(Once bitten, twice shy)

1798
01:00:08,360 --> 01:00:08,840
No.

1799
01:00:08,840 --> 01:00:09,840
See what else is there.

1800
01:00:10,280 --> 01:00:10,920
There's only WeChat.

1801
01:00:12,040 --> 01:00:12,720
Group chats?

1802
01:00:13,440 --> 01:00:15,240
Or bills? A wallet?

1803
01:00:15,240 --> 01:00:16,560
(Nothing at all)

1804
01:00:16,560 --> 01:00:17,720
Alright. Let's

1805
01:00:17,720 --> 01:00:18,920
start the interrogation.

1806
01:00:18,920 --> 01:00:20,520
Let's each figure out

1807
01:00:20,520 --> 01:00:22,000
who the culprit is.

1808
01:00:22,560 --> 01:00:23,240
Let's go back and...

1809
01:00:23,240 --> 01:00:23,960
We'll talk back there.

1810
01:00:23,960 --> 01:00:24,400
Let's go.

1811
01:00:25,440 --> 01:00:26,800
I really think it's the capybara.

1812
01:00:26,800 --> 01:00:27,880
(Absolutely certain)
You don't believe me.

1813
01:00:28,360 --> 01:00:31,240
Come on. Let's just vote.

1814
01:00:31,240 --> 01:00:32,640
Vote for me.

1815
01:00:32,640 --> 01:00:33,760
See? He's doing it again.

1816
01:00:34,280 --> 01:00:36,840
We're not falling for it.

1817
01:00:36,840 --> 01:00:37,840
He does this every time.

1818
01:00:37,840 --> 01:00:39,560
I've seen it way too many times.

1819
01:00:39,560 --> 01:00:41,760
Yeah. Whenever someone suspects him,

1820
01:00:41,760 --> 01:00:44,600
he goes, "Vote for me. Come on".

1821
01:00:44,600 --> 01:00:45,680
Exactly.

1822
01:00:45,680 --> 01:00:46,760
Okay.

1823
01:00:46,760 --> 01:00:48,620
(Which one of them is the culprit?)

1824
01:00:53,880 --> 01:00:54,960
Longdong Army!

1825
01:00:55,760 --> 01:00:56,760
Longdong Army!

1826
01:00:57,080 --> 01:00:58,360
(Fired up instantly)
Longdong Army!

1827
01:00:58,360 --> 01:00:59,480
Longdong Army!

1828
01:00:59,720 --> 01:01:01,600
(Everything becomes Longdong Army)
Longdong Army!

1829
01:01:03,720 --> 01:01:06,200
(Wrap it up)
Let's question a suspect first.

1830
01:01:06,200 --> 01:01:07,880
Let's bring in...

1831
01:01:07,880 --> 01:01:08,640
Bu Kakao?

1832
01:01:09,120 --> 01:01:09,960
(Bu Kepa)
Welcome, Bu Ka...

1833
01:01:09,960 --> 01:01:11,560
Bu Ka...

1834
01:01:12,280 --> 01:01:13,360
Bu Ka...

1835
01:01:13,360 --> 01:01:14,220
(Don't get tongue-tied!)
Bu Kakao.

1836
01:01:14,220 --> 01:01:14,920
Tongue-tied.

1837
01:01:14,920 --> 01:01:16,320
See? His name makes me tongue-tied.

1838
01:01:18,360 --> 01:01:20,960
Bu Kakao, take a seat.

1839
01:01:21,380 --> 01:01:24,620
(Tui Games Company secretary,
Bu Kakao, played by Li Bangbang)

1840
01:01:24,920 --> 01:01:25,360
Here he comes.

1841
01:01:25,840 --> 01:01:26,320
Come on.

1842
01:01:27,040 --> 01:01:27,760
Come in.

1843
01:01:28,160 --> 01:01:28,520
Over here.

1844
01:01:28,520 --> 01:01:28,940
(Detective intimidation)

1845
01:01:29,600 --> 01:01:30,560
Why do you have a weapon?

1846
01:01:31,120 --> 01:01:32,360
You can speak human, right?

1847
01:01:32,360 --> 01:01:33,560
Yes, I can speak human.

1848
01:01:33,920 --> 01:01:35,240
As long as you tell the truth,

1849
01:01:35,240 --> 01:01:37,400
the bullet won't go through your chest.

1850
01:01:38,400 --> 01:01:39,560
Okay.

1851
01:01:39,560 --> 01:01:41,760
Stand up. Let's find...

1852
01:01:41,760 --> 01:01:43,040
(The detectives start frisking him)
What's this? A mosquito patch?

1853
01:01:43,040 --> 01:01:43,880
Yes. That's...

1854
01:01:43,880 --> 01:01:44,320
Mine.

1855
01:01:44,840 --> 01:01:46,520
(All the detectives join in)
You humans are very thorough.

1856
01:01:47,920 --> 01:01:49,400
I saw some paper in his back pocket.

1857
01:01:49,840 --> 01:01:50,520
His back pocket.

1858
01:01:50,520 --> 01:01:51,240
(Searching carefully)

1859
01:01:51,240 --> 01:01:52,000
Nothing.

1860
01:01:52,440 --> 01:01:53,160
Where is it? You...

1861
01:01:53,160 --> 01:01:54,240
There's really nothing.

1862
01:01:54,640 --> 01:01:55,040
Nothing.

1863
01:01:55,720 --> 01:01:57,040
I only have my tail.

1864
01:01:57,240 --> 01:01:58,480
Is there anything inside your tail?

1865
01:01:59,560 --> 01:01:59,920
No.

1866
01:02:00,760 --> 01:02:01,520
No.

1867
01:02:01,520 --> 01:02:02,900
(No evidence found)

1868
01:02:03,360 --> 01:02:04,080
(Giving up)
Sit down.

1869
01:02:05,720 --> 01:02:06,840
What do you want to ask me?

1870
01:02:07,720 --> 01:02:09,880
(Group questioning: 10-minute limit)
Did you and Tui Haowan

1871
01:02:09,880 --> 01:02:11,000
have

1872
01:02:11,000 --> 01:02:13,080
some kind of secret plan?

1873
01:02:13,560 --> 01:02:15,280
Did he tell you to scare people

1874
01:02:15,280 --> 01:02:17,760
at 2:30, 2:45, or 3PM?

1875
01:02:17,760 --> 01:02:18,720
To frighten them?

1876
01:02:19,800 --> 01:02:22,000
Actually, that's true.

1877
01:02:22,800 --> 01:02:26,200
Mr. Tui told me to scare the humans.

1878
01:02:26,200 --> 01:02:26,680
Right.

1879
01:02:26,680 --> 01:02:28,680
So they'd stop bullying the animals.

1880
01:02:28,680 --> 01:02:30,640
I've got a recording of you and him.

1881
01:02:31,000 --> 01:02:32,960
(Bu Kakao, June 21, 2026, 3PM)
Bu, do exactly as I say.

1882
01:02:33,240 --> 01:02:35,200
Mark the courtyard breaker box.

1883
01:02:35,400 --> 01:02:37,000
Make sure you use

1884
01:02:37,000 --> 01:02:38,680
an invisible UV marker.

1885
01:02:39,200 --> 01:02:41,720
What did he tell you to do
at the breaker box?

1886
01:02:42,240 --> 01:02:44,120
Yes. He told me to

1887
01:02:44,120 --> 01:02:46,200
mark something inside it.

1888
01:02:46,960 --> 01:02:47,720
Did you go?

1889
01:02:47,720 --> 01:02:48,520
Did you?

1890
01:02:48,520 --> 01:02:49,640
I did.

1891
01:02:49,640 --> 01:02:52,040
I had to do what my boss said.

1892
01:02:52,360 --> 01:02:54,040
(Tui Haowan masterminded the scare plan)
So you wrote those words, right?

1893
01:02:54,240 --> 01:02:55,920
Yes. I wrote those words.

1894
01:02:55,920 --> 01:02:57,680
(Do not touch. Electric shock hazard)
"Do not touch. Electric shock hazard".

1895
01:02:57,680 --> 01:02:58,880
Electric shock hazard.

1896
01:02:58,880 --> 01:03:02,720
So you bought that UV marker, right?

1897
01:03:02,720 --> 01:03:04,800
It belongs to my boss.

1898
01:03:04,800 --> 01:03:06,080
(The UV light belongs to Tui Haowan)
How many UV pens did you see?

1899
01:03:06,560 --> 01:03:09,520
Just this one UV light.

1900
01:03:09,520 --> 01:03:10,640
(Only one UV light in Tui's office)
Only one UV pen?

1901
01:03:10,640 --> 01:03:10,960
Yes.

1902
01:03:10,960 --> 01:03:13,240
After you used the tools,

1903
01:03:13,240 --> 01:03:14,960
did you put them back?

1904
01:03:14,960 --> 01:03:15,640
I did.

1905
01:03:15,640 --> 01:03:19,280
But this morning,

1906
01:03:19,720 --> 01:03:21,400
I went back to my boss' desk

1907
01:03:21,400 --> 01:03:23,720
and found that the UV light

1908
01:03:23,720 --> 01:03:28,160
and the breaker key had been moved.

1909
01:03:28,220 --> 01:03:31,980
(Bu Kakao's testimony: Someone moved
both the UV light and the key)

1910
01:03:32,000 --> 01:03:34,520
They weren't where
I'd left them yesterday.

1911
01:03:34,680 --> 01:03:36,360
So someone moved them, right?

1912
01:03:36,360 --> 01:03:36,880
Yes.

1913
01:03:36,880 --> 01:03:37,280
Pretty much.

1914
01:03:37,620 --> 01:03:39,740
(Confirmed: Someone changed the
marked position on the breaker box)

1915
01:03:40,600 --> 01:03:42,000
Something just occurred to me.

1916
01:03:42,000 --> 01:03:44,040
You were planning this whole thing

1917
01:03:44,040 --> 01:03:45,040
with your boss, right?

1918
01:03:45,040 --> 01:03:45,680
Yes.

1919
01:03:45,680 --> 01:03:47,440
One part of the plan was

1920
01:03:47,440 --> 01:03:49,760
to cut the power

1921
01:03:49,760 --> 01:03:51,320
and then scare us, right?

1922
01:03:51,320 --> 01:03:51,640
Yes.

1923
01:03:51,640 --> 01:03:55,640
Did you ever say that

1924
01:03:55,640 --> 01:03:58,760
if we hid in that cabinet,

1925
01:03:58,760 --> 01:04:00,480
we wouldn't get scared?

1926
01:04:00,640 --> 01:04:04,160
(Urban legend)
Here's how to survive.

1927
01:04:04,160 --> 01:04:05,120
If there's a cabinet nearby

1928
01:04:05,120 --> 01:04:08,520
(Leaf icon for warding off bad luck)
with this leaf symbol on it...

1929
01:04:08,520 --> 01:04:10,040
Hide inside alone,

1930
01:04:10,040 --> 01:04:12,080
and you'll be safe.

1931
01:04:13,080 --> 01:04:14,960
Honestly, I

1932
01:04:14,960 --> 01:04:17,680
didn't expect that today.

1933
01:04:17,680 --> 01:04:19,520
I didn't think you'd hide in there.

1934
01:04:19,620 --> 01:04:24,620
(Hiding in the cabinet wasn't
part of Tui Haowan's plan)

1935
01:04:24,840 --> 01:04:27,360
And that leaf symbol

1936
01:04:27,360 --> 01:04:28,560
(Guiding symbol on the cabinet)
wasn't drawn by you either?

1937
01:04:32,240 --> 01:04:33,240
So that note

1938
01:04:33,240 --> 01:04:34,760
telling us to go inside...

1939
01:04:34,760 --> 01:04:36,040
(The note wasn't part of Tui's plan)
Wasn't theirs either?

1940
01:04:36,640 --> 01:04:38,160
The killer planted it.

1941
01:04:39,280 --> 01:04:40,480
The killer needed to get out,

1942
01:04:40,480 --> 01:04:42,440
so they got us all inside first.

1943
01:04:42,460 --> 01:04:44,700
(Theory: The note telling them
to hide in the cabinet)

1944
01:04:44,700 --> 01:04:47,060
(was planted by the killer
to establish an alibi)

1945
01:04:47,080 --> 01:04:49,720
Is there anything else we don't know

1946
01:04:49,720 --> 01:04:51,600
(Leading deduction)
that you'd like to tell us?

1947
01:04:51,800 --> 01:04:53,840
Here's the thing.

1948
01:04:53,840 --> 01:04:56,360
I really was trying to save everyone.

1949
01:04:56,720 --> 01:04:57,200
Of course.

1950
01:04:57,560 --> 01:04:59,120
If anything happens,

1951
01:04:59,280 --> 01:05:00,440
run with me.

1952
01:05:01,760 --> 01:05:03,080
Why are you talking to me?

1953
01:05:03,240 --> 01:05:04,120
Hurry! Follow me!

1954
01:05:04,680 --> 01:05:05,120
Run!

1955
01:05:05,680 --> 01:05:07,760
Seeing that no one trusted me

1956
01:05:07,760 --> 01:05:08,800
hurt a little.

1957
01:05:08,800 --> 01:05:10,680
But everyone else doubted me,

1958
01:05:10,680 --> 01:05:11,360
and I put up with it.

1959
01:05:12,120 --> 01:05:13,280
Even you didn't believe me.

1960
01:05:13,460 --> 01:05:14,740
(Jin Goofy freezes)

1961
01:05:14,820 --> 01:05:16,780
(What's Jin Goofy's
connection to Bu Kakao?)

1962
01:05:16,800 --> 01:05:17,240
Who?

1963
01:05:17,840 --> 01:05:19,280
Do you remember me,

1964
01:05:19,560 --> 01:05:20,240
Aunt Jin?

1965
01:05:20,580 --> 01:05:22,780
(Aunt Jin?)

1966
01:05:23,160 --> 01:05:24,000
I don't remember.

1967
01:05:24,920 --> 01:05:26,200
I'm Little Woofy.

1968
01:05:26,440 --> 01:05:27,440
Little Woofy?

1969
01:05:27,440 --> 01:05:28,440
I was one of your dogs.

1970
01:05:28,440 --> 01:05:30,520
My dad and I were both your dogs.

1971
01:05:31,800 --> 01:05:32,960
Didn't you raise golden retrievers?

1972
01:05:34,520 --> 01:05:36,360
I think Aunt Jin abused dogs.

1973
01:05:36,360 --> 01:05:37,560
Yeah. You abused dogs.

1974
01:05:37,560 --> 01:05:39,480
(Woofy (Bu Kakao's dad))
She said she liked me.

1975
01:05:39,480 --> 01:05:41,640
(AI-generated. Don't imitate)
Even the harshest light,

1976
01:05:41,640 --> 01:05:42,800
(No animal abuse)
I'd endure.

1977
01:05:43,080 --> 01:05:44,920
Then I noticed

1978
01:05:44,920 --> 01:05:46,640
some new employees had joined,

1979
01:05:46,640 --> 01:05:47,520
including you.

1980
01:05:48,080 --> 01:05:49,040
But I also knew

1981
01:05:49,040 --> 01:05:51,200
Mr. Tui was up to no good.

1982
01:05:51,800 --> 01:05:54,120
So I wanted to protect you in secret.

1983
01:05:54,360 --> 01:05:56,120
The moment I saw you,

1984
01:05:56,120 --> 01:05:57,080
you felt so familiar.

1985
01:05:57,080 --> 01:05:58,240
I kept wanting to be near you.

1986
01:05:58,440 --> 01:05:59,520
But you didn't believe me!

1987
01:06:01,040 --> 01:06:01,680
I believe you now.

1988
01:06:01,680 --> 01:06:02,240
I forgot.

1989
01:06:02,240 --> 01:06:03,680
Come on. Shake.

1990
01:06:03,680 --> 01:06:04,280
(Core programming activated)
Okay, left paw.

1991
01:06:04,840 --> 01:06:05,240
Good.

1992
01:06:10,040 --> 01:06:11,640
Did you want to protect her?

1993
01:06:11,640 --> 01:06:12,760
Yes, of course.

1994
01:06:12,960 --> 01:06:16,240
Before my dad passed, he told me

1995
01:06:16,240 --> 01:06:18,240
that dogs

1996
01:06:18,240 --> 01:06:21,240
must always be loyal to their owners.

1997
01:06:23,260 --> 01:06:25,500
(Little Woofy will always love Aunt Jin)

1998
01:06:25,800 --> 01:06:27,360
Never forget your owner.

1999
01:06:28,220 --> 01:06:30,460
(Give Little Woofy his favorite bone)

2000
01:06:32,600 --> 01:06:34,440
I'm kind of touched.

2001
01:06:34,440 --> 01:06:35,660
(Emotional little bunny)

2002
01:06:35,880 --> 01:06:37,440
So will you stay with me?

2003
01:06:37,440 --> 01:06:38,720
(Prove my innocence)
You can prove I'm innocent.

2004
01:06:39,880 --> 01:06:41,680
Like when I was locked in the cabinet,

2005
01:06:41,680 --> 01:06:42,800
you would've protected me,

2006
01:06:42,800 --> 01:06:44,240
or at least not scared me on purpose.

2007
01:06:44,240 --> 01:06:45,760
Doesn't that rule me out?

2008
01:06:47,280 --> 01:06:48,680
I wanted to protect you so badly

2009
01:06:48,680 --> 01:06:50,520
that I told you the whole plan.

2010
01:06:50,520 --> 01:06:51,400
Just lock me in.

2011
01:06:51,400 --> 01:06:54,480
He came in and openly named me,

2012
01:06:54,480 --> 01:06:55,960
then locked me in.

2013
01:06:55,960 --> 01:06:57,000
Guys!

2014
01:06:58,240 --> 01:07:00,480
No, I think we can rule her out.

2015
01:07:00,580 --> 01:07:01,780
(At least Ke's on my side)

2016
01:07:02,040 --> 01:07:03,040
Rule out who?

2017
01:07:03,400 --> 01:07:04,360
Him.

2018
01:07:06,200 --> 01:07:07,480
(Rule out Bu Kakao)
We can rule him out, of course.

2019
01:07:07,800 --> 01:07:09,080
Of course.

2020
01:07:10,040 --> 01:07:11,000
After all that talking,

2021
01:07:11,280 --> 01:07:13,760
I meant rule me out! Ning, ask him.

2022
01:07:14,080 --> 01:07:15,720
We never suspected him.

2023
01:07:15,960 --> 01:07:16,680
Right.

2024
01:07:16,680 --> 01:07:17,960
He's just a little dog.

2025
01:07:17,960 --> 01:07:19,720
Exactly. Just a puppy.

2026
01:07:19,720 --> 01:07:20,340
(A puppy trusts another puppy)
Puppy.

2027
01:07:20,380 --> 01:07:22,240
(One innocent little puppy)

2028
01:07:22,240 --> 01:07:23,800
Alright, you're good. You can go.

2029
01:07:23,800 --> 01:07:24,720
Thanks for your help.

2030
01:07:24,720 --> 01:07:25,160
Okay.

2031
01:07:25,160 --> 01:07:25,480
Good.

2032
01:07:25,480 --> 01:07:26,240
Keep it up.

2033
01:07:26,240 --> 01:07:28,120
(Bu Kakao's interrogation ends)
I'll take care of you.

2034
01:07:28,120 --> 01:07:28,840
I'm off!

2035
01:07:29,200 --> 01:07:29,680
Okay.

2036
01:07:30,480 --> 01:07:32,400
Okay, so now,

2037
01:07:32,400 --> 01:07:34,480
(Accent slips)
what was the point of bringing him in?

2038
01:07:34,480 --> 01:07:36,800
(Summary of Bu Kakao's testimony:)
First, he confirmed that the tools

2039
01:07:36,800 --> 01:07:38,440
(1. UV light and breaker key were moved)
had been moved.

2040
01:07:38,440 --> 01:07:41,160
Also, the killer arranged
all the cabinets,

2041
01:07:41,160 --> 01:07:42,880
and made up the whole story.

2042
01:07:42,880 --> 01:07:44,100
(2. Theory: "Survival Guide"
and single-person cabinets)

2043
01:07:44,100 --> 01:07:45,100
(were deliberately set up by the killer)

2044
01:07:45,840 --> 01:07:46,880
We've considered so much,

2045
01:07:46,880 --> 01:07:47,880
but forgot one thing.

2046
01:07:48,920 --> 01:07:49,800
To find out

2047
01:07:49,800 --> 01:07:51,760
about Mr. Tui's prank,

2048
01:07:52,280 --> 01:07:54,840
the person's job matters.

2049
01:07:54,840 --> 01:07:56,160
(Argument about the killer:)
Did they have the chance?

2050
01:07:56,160 --> 01:07:57,120
(Whose job)
Let's start with mine.

2051
01:07:57,120 --> 01:07:57,840
(Could reveal Tui Haowan's prank plan?)
I do motion capture.

2052
01:07:58,800 --> 01:08:00,760
(He Struggle, motion capture artist)
My partner's a game designer.

2053
01:08:00,760 --> 01:08:01,440
(Nan Shy, game designer)
We share an office.

2054
01:08:01,440 --> 01:08:04,240
We rarely get to interact
with him directly.

2055
01:08:04,260 --> 01:08:05,100
(He Struggle and Nan Shy's
defense: Their jobs)

2056
01:08:05,100 --> 01:08:06,180
(Give them little access
to Tui Haowan or his prank plan)

2057
01:08:06,800 --> 01:08:08,320
What was his job again?

2058
01:08:08,320 --> 01:08:09,240
Game streamer.

2059
01:08:09,240 --> 01:08:10,680
(Ke Uh-Oh, game streamer)
Game streamer.

2060
01:08:10,680 --> 01:08:11,760
He'd have chances too.

2061
01:08:12,280 --> 01:08:14,240
(Boss stays close during streams)
The boss would stand behind him

2062
01:08:14,240 --> 01:08:15,320
and pull his hair.

2063
01:08:15,320 --> 01:08:17,000
(Ke Uh-Oh, game streamer, had access)
Her job gives her access too.

2064
01:08:17,000 --> 01:08:17,680
Even more.

2065
01:08:17,779 --> 01:08:18,680
(Jin Goofy, HR manager, had access)
HR manager.

2066
01:08:18,680 --> 01:08:20,040
(Jin Goofy, private performer)
She also gives private performances.

2067
01:08:20,819 --> 01:08:22,020
(He Struggle's suspects:
Ke Uh-Oh and Jin Goofy)

2068
01:08:22,020 --> 01:08:23,160
(Reason: Their jobs gave them
easier access to Tui Haowan)

2069
01:08:23,160 --> 01:08:24,439
I think our top priority

2070
01:08:24,439 --> 01:08:26,240
is questioning the other person.

2071
01:08:26,240 --> 01:08:27,319
Sure, no problem.

2072
01:08:27,319 --> 01:08:29,520
Let's bring in Tai Kule.

2073
01:08:29,819 --> 01:08:30,960
(Tai Kule arrives for questioning)

2074
01:08:30,960 --> 01:08:32,840
He was also one of the two
who scared us.

2075
01:08:33,319 --> 01:08:34,680
Stand here. Let me search you first.

2076
01:08:35,100 --> 01:08:38,100
(Routine detective pat-down)

2077
01:08:38,939 --> 01:08:40,779
(Thorough search)

2078
01:08:42,640 --> 01:08:43,560
Are you done yet?

2079
01:08:43,560 --> 01:08:44,359
(Even a suspect bear has limits)
Fine, go ahead.

2080
01:08:44,359 --> 01:08:44,920
That should be everything.

2081
01:08:45,020 --> 01:08:45,899
(No evidence found)

2082
01:08:46,319 --> 01:08:47,200
Okay, have a seat.

2083
01:08:48,160 --> 01:08:49,800
There's something I want to ask.

2084
01:08:49,800 --> 01:08:51,240
You helped us just now.

2085
01:08:51,240 --> 01:08:51,720
Why?

2086
01:08:53,560 --> 01:08:55,120
Go!

2087
01:08:55,120 --> 01:08:56,080
Run! Hurry!

2088
01:08:56,920 --> 01:08:58,960
Because I felt sorry for you.

2089
01:08:58,960 --> 01:09:00,520
That situation was really dangerous.

2090
01:09:00,920 --> 01:09:02,319
So you're just pure-hearted?

2091
01:09:02,760 --> 01:09:04,359
He's just a kind person.

2092
01:09:04,359 --> 01:09:06,120
Do you know what the six of us did?

2093
01:09:06,120 --> 01:09:07,359
We used to abuse animals.

2094
01:09:07,359 --> 01:09:08,359
(Shocking revelation for the kind bear)
That's why we're locked up here.

2095
01:09:08,359 --> 01:09:09,520
We're being punished.

2096
01:09:09,760 --> 01:09:10,840
I don't care

2097
01:09:10,840 --> 01:09:12,640
what you did before.

2098
01:09:12,960 --> 01:09:14,080
But in this place,

2099
01:09:14,080 --> 01:09:16,080
no one should abuse people or animals.

2100
01:09:19,439 --> 01:09:20,319
Thank you.

2101
01:09:20,319 --> 01:09:21,960
I'm

2102
01:09:21,960 --> 01:09:23,120
the most righteous bear.

2103
01:09:23,120 --> 01:09:24,439
(Embodiment of kindness and justice)

2104
01:09:24,439 --> 01:09:26,520
Right, you already know all that.

2105
01:09:26,520 --> 01:09:27,560
I'm a bear.

2106
01:09:27,560 --> 01:09:28,920
After I got the injection,

2107
01:09:28,920 --> 01:09:30,399
I took on a human form.

2108
01:09:30,920 --> 01:09:31,240
Right.

2109
01:09:31,720 --> 01:09:34,920
So today, over in Animal World,

2110
01:09:34,920 --> 01:09:35,520
you were hanging around there.

2111
01:09:35,520 --> 01:09:36,359
When we spotted you,

2112
01:09:36,359 --> 01:09:36,920
what were you doing?

2113
01:09:37,760 --> 01:09:39,479
I was watching to see what they'd do.

2114
01:09:39,960 --> 01:09:40,960
Was that your first time there?

2115
01:09:40,960 --> 01:09:41,960
It was.

2116
01:09:41,960 --> 01:09:43,520
I've been to this place before,

2117
01:09:43,520 --> 01:09:45,880
but I'd never entered that secret room.

2118
01:09:46,240 --> 01:09:48,359
I always suspected something
was wrong there.

2119
01:09:49,160 --> 01:09:51,359
So I risked my life today

2120
01:09:51,359 --> 01:09:52,439
and went in to investigate.

2121
01:09:52,760 --> 01:09:54,800
Turns out something really was wrong.

2122
01:09:55,480 --> 01:09:56,360
It was so cruel!

2123
01:09:57,360 --> 01:09:58,200
It went way too far!

2124
01:09:58,840 --> 01:10:01,640
While you were talking to Mr. Tui,

2125
01:10:01,640 --> 01:10:02,920
did you realize something was wrong?

2126
01:10:03,080 --> 01:10:04,080
Of course I did.

2127
01:10:04,080 --> 01:10:05,520
We went to college together.

2128
01:10:05,680 --> 01:10:07,320
Animals have colleges too?

2129
01:10:08,720 --> 01:10:10,040
(Clearly offended)
We...

2130
01:10:10,040 --> 01:10:11,160
We're highly advanced!

2131
01:10:11,160 --> 01:10:13,960
(Kind but short-tempered bear)
We're way more advanced than you!

2132
01:10:14,400 --> 01:10:16,040
He's from a higher dimension.

2133
01:10:16,760 --> 01:10:17,560
Got it.

2134
01:10:17,560 --> 01:10:18,340
(Didn't see that coming)

2135
01:10:18,800 --> 01:10:19,640
So then?

2136
01:10:19,640 --> 01:10:20,600
Go on.

2137
01:10:20,600 --> 01:10:21,560
You two were college classmates.

2138
01:10:21,560 --> 01:10:23,040
Yes, we were.

2139
01:10:23,560 --> 01:10:25,600
(Tai Kule and Tui were classmates)
After he took charge here,

2140
01:10:25,600 --> 01:10:28,480
I slowly became involved
with this company.

2141
01:10:29,120 --> 01:10:30,280
We do punish

2142
01:10:30,280 --> 01:10:31,880
humans who've abused animals.

2143
01:10:32,880 --> 01:10:33,480
But

2144
01:10:34,360 --> 01:10:36,000
sometimes I noticed

2145
01:10:36,000 --> 01:10:37,840
that if a hundred people went in,

2146
01:10:37,840 --> 01:10:39,640
only about sixty came back out.

2147
01:10:39,900 --> 01:10:41,160
(Mr. Tui has punished
a huge number of humans)

2148
01:10:41,160 --> 01:10:42,440
That was a major problem.

2149
01:10:42,440 --> 01:10:43,280
Something was fishy.

2150
01:10:43,280 --> 01:10:45,080
I kept wondering
where the other forty went.

2151
01:10:45,080 --> 01:10:46,160
So you came to investigate.

2152
01:10:46,160 --> 01:10:47,800
I came to find out what was going on.

2153
01:10:47,820 --> 01:10:48,880
(Detective Bear is on the case)

2154
01:10:48,880 --> 01:10:50,560
That's how I found that place.

2155
01:10:50,560 --> 01:10:51,240
I found it.

2156
01:10:51,240 --> 01:10:52,880
Then you guys came in.

2157
01:10:52,880 --> 01:10:53,720
When you walked in,

2158
01:10:53,720 --> 01:10:54,440
didn't I keep trying

2159
01:10:54,440 --> 01:10:55,600
to signal you with my eyes?

2160
01:10:57,500 --> 01:11:00,220
(Signaling with his eyes)

2161
01:11:00,220 --> 01:11:02,140
(Shaking his head as a warning)

2162
01:11:02,280 --> 01:11:05,520
Do you approve of what Mr. Tui did?

2163
01:11:05,520 --> 01:11:06,360
Of course not.

2164
01:11:06,360 --> 01:11:06,960
Of course you don't.

2165
01:11:06,960 --> 01:11:08,280
Since you don't approve,

2166
01:11:08,280 --> 01:11:09,720
do you want to punish him?

2167
01:11:10,760 --> 01:11:11,520
Honestly,

2168
01:11:11,520 --> 01:11:13,160
I never wanted to punish him.

2169
01:11:13,160 --> 01:11:14,080
I just thought

2170
01:11:14,080 --> 01:11:16,240
if this really happened,

2171
01:11:16,240 --> 01:11:18,320
I'd report it to the Animal Bureau.

2172
01:11:18,320 --> 01:11:18,800
You know,

2173
01:11:18,800 --> 01:11:19,840
fighting violence with violence

2174
01:11:19,840 --> 01:11:21,400
is never the right answer.

2175
01:11:21,840 --> 01:11:23,280
So if someone told you,

2176
01:11:23,280 --> 01:11:25,600
"I want to kill Mr. Tui today".

2177
01:11:25,600 --> 01:11:26,800
"Let's work together, "

2178
01:11:26,800 --> 01:11:28,560
you wouldn't agree?

2179
01:11:28,560 --> 01:11:29,960
Of course I wouldn't.

2180
01:11:29,960 --> 01:11:30,840
No matter what,

2181
01:11:31,360 --> 01:11:33,200
he was wrong, but
he didn't deserve to die.

2182
01:11:33,200 --> 01:11:34,360
But Tui Haowan told you,

2183
01:11:34,360 --> 01:11:35,440
"At 3PM today, "

2184
01:11:35,440 --> 01:11:37,480
"I'm gonna scare these
six people to death".

2185
01:11:37,480 --> 01:11:38,640
Why did you agree?

2186
01:11:44,880 --> 01:11:46,360
When did I agree
to scare six people to death?

2187
01:11:47,280 --> 01:11:49,240
Weren't you two there at 3PM?

2188
01:11:49,240 --> 01:11:50,040
Tui Haowan?

2189
01:11:51,120 --> 01:11:52,360
It wasn't Tui Haowan.

2190
01:11:52,380 --> 01:11:54,140
(Was someone else behind the scare?)

2191
01:11:57,560 --> 01:12:00,040
Bu Kakao dragged me along to scare them.

2192
01:12:00,040 --> 01:12:01,560
What does Tui Haowan have to do with it?

2193
01:12:04,040 --> 01:12:06,680
What did he tell you?

2194
01:12:06,680 --> 01:12:08,360
Why did you agree to scare people?

2195
01:12:08,960 --> 01:12:10,280
Because I needed to get in.

2196
01:12:10,280 --> 01:12:11,720
I don't work here.

2197
01:12:11,720 --> 01:12:12,960
I don't have clearance either.

2198
01:12:12,960 --> 01:12:14,520
I couldn't just walk in.

2199
01:12:14,960 --> 01:12:16,280
So I told him

2200
01:12:16,280 --> 01:12:19,240
I wanted to use
this gathering to get inside.

2201
01:12:19,680 --> 01:12:21,560
He said, "Sure, no problem".

2202
01:12:21,560 --> 01:12:22,400
Then he said, "Come with me"

2203
01:12:22,400 --> 01:12:23,760
"and help me scare them".

2204
01:12:23,760 --> 01:12:25,760
"It's a punishment humans too".

2205
01:12:25,780 --> 01:12:27,860
(He had to scare everyone
to investigate the missing humans)

2206
01:12:28,040 --> 01:12:28,520
Got it.

2207
01:12:28,800 --> 01:12:29,360
Alright.

2208
01:12:29,840 --> 01:12:31,120
Okay, thanks for your time.

2209
01:12:31,120 --> 01:12:32,160
Alright. We're done here.

2210
01:12:32,160 --> 01:12:34,320
Make sure you catch the real killer.

2211
01:12:34,320 --> 01:12:35,040
Catch them.

2212
01:12:35,040 --> 01:12:36,320
(Tai Kule's interrogation ends)

2213
01:12:36,320 --> 01:12:37,600
Anyone else to question?

2214
01:12:37,600 --> 01:12:38,160
Nope.

2215
01:12:38,680 --> 01:12:40,360
